        "original_id": "c516c4a0-042c-5f2e-b390-e1df6f93c6c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: French suburbs, banlieues, France\n- Concepts: troubled suburban communities, Black people in France, foreign origin, Black African ancestry, Afro-Caribbean ancestry\n- Topics: unemployment, crime rates, immigration from former French African colonies\n\nFacts:\n- In France, the term banlieues has often been used to describe troubled suburban communities.\n- Troubled banlieues are described as having high unemployment and high crime rates.\n- Troubled banlieues are also described as frequently having a high proportion of residents of foreign origin, mainly from former French African colonies, including Berbers, Blacks, and Arabs.\n- In France, Black people or Noirs de France are people of Black African ancestry or Afro-Caribbean ancestry.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
